---
id: turkey-three-bean-chili
title: Turkey Three-Bean Chili
category: one_dish

yield:
  servings: 4
  cooked_g: 2600

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: true

---

Heat @olive-oil{1%tsp} in a #large-pot over medium-high heat. Add @extra-lean-ground-turkey{1%package} and cook for ~brown{6%minute}, breaking it into small pieces, until no pink remains.

Add @yellow-onion{1}, diced, and @mixed-bell-peppers{1}, diced, and cook for ~soften{5%minute} until the onion is soft and translucent.

Stir in @fresh-garlic{3%clove}, minced, with @chili-powder{1 1/2%tbsp}, @ground-cumin{1%tsp}, @smoked-paprika{1%tsp}, @dried-oregano{1/2%tsp}, and @ground-cayenne{1/8%tsp} (the tiny kick; add more next time if you like). Cook for ~toast{1%minute}, stirring, until fragrant. Stir in the whole can of @tomato-paste{1%package} and cook for ~paste{1%minute} more.

Drain and rinse @organic-pinto-beans{1%package}, @longos-organic-black-beans{1%package}, and @longos-organic-kidney-beans{1%package} in a colander. Add them to the pot with @canned-diced-tomatoes{1%package} and their juice, @frozen-sweet-corn{1/2%cup}, and 1 cup of water. Season with @kosher-salt{1/2%tsp} and @black-pepper{1/4%tsp}.

Bring to a boil, then cover, lower the heat to medium-low, and simmer for ~simmer{30%minute}, stirring now and then so the bottom doesn't catch. Taste and add salt if needed; the low-sodium beans and no-salt tomatoes bring little, so this is where you set it. Add a splash of water if it gets thicker than you like; it thickens more as it cools.

Divide into 4 containers. Refrigerate 2 for the next days and freeze 2; they keep 3 to 4 months frozen. Thaw a frozen portion in the fridge overnight, or microwave it from frozen, stirring halfway.

To serve, reheat until steaming and top each bowl with 50 g of @greek-yogurt-2pct{200%g}, 15 g of @light-old-cheddar{60%g} grated, and thinly sliced @green-onions{1/4%bunch}, all added fresh after reheating.
